1
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:22,100
Huh?

2
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:24,660
Where am I?

3
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:31,560
Wait, did I fall asleep?

4
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:36,240
Well...

5
00:00:38,110 --> 00:00:40,640
[Coin changer]

6
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,800
I really did...

7
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:44,580
pass out while I was hanging out

8
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:46,180
[Coin changer]

9
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,460
with everyone.

10
00:00:57,490 --> 00:00:58,340
Ren.

11
00:00:58,370 --> 00:00:59,620
-Ren!
-Ren!

12
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:00,710
Are you okay?

13
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:01,590
-Are you okay?
-Ren.

14
00:01:01,590 --> 00:01:02,280
Ren.

15
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:08,340
Issei.

16
00:01:08,890 --> 00:01:09,660
Ren!

17
00:01:09,690 --> 00:01:11,260
Are you okay?

18
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:13,350
Ren!

19
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:15,800
-Ren!
-Wake up.

20
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:18,370
-What happened after that?
-Ren, Ren.

21
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:27,340
Did I...

22
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:30,789
get hit somewhere fatal and die?

23
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:39,200
If so,

24
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,300
then this place must be...

25
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:42,580
Heaven.

26
00:01:43,509 --> 00:01:44,560
Oh.

27
00:01:45,330 --> 00:01:48,150
But this feels so real.

28
00:01:52,470 --> 00:01:53,320
You're awake.

29
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,479
Hey, why are you here?

30
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:05,930
Because this is my place.

31
00:02:08,449 --> 00:02:10,250
Then this is...

32
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:12,930
That's right.

33
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:15,670
It's my bed.

34
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,340
Could it be...

35
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:22,920
Wait, did we sleep together?

36
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:28,190
Huh?

37
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:36,550
♪ Through the crack in the window ♪

38
00:02:36,570 --> 00:02:40,460
♪ Summer sunlight streams on down ♪

39
00:02:40,490 --> 00:02:44,750
♪ OH YEAH, beneath the endless blue sky ♪

40
00:02:44,770 --> 00:02:48,110
♪ I make a promise deep inside, YEAH ♪

41
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,550
♪ From today on,
I'll fill the pages with my thoughts ♪

42
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:52,530
♪ Along with all those silly words ♪

43
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:55,820
♪ I'm just one step away from you ♪

44
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,220
♪ One little leap is all it takes ♪

45
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:00,210
♪ Before the summer comes to an end ♪

46
00:03:00,210 --> 00:03:03,640
♪ I'll leave my mark on your heart ♪

47
00:03:03,670 --> 00:03:05,750
♪ 'Cause I feel the breeze ♪

48
00:03:05,770 --> 00:03:07,670
♪ Only this moment matters ♪

49
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:10,990
♪ I make a wish upon the heavens ♪

50
00:03:11,010 --> 00:03:14,320
♪ OK, as for tomorrow ♪

51
00:03:14,350 --> 00:03:19,120
♪ Let tomorrow's wind take care of it ♪

52
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:22,910
♪ YEAH, open up this door ♪

53
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:26,829
♪ And let's set off together ♪

54
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:29,820
♪ Summer vibe, no tomorrow, summer vibe ♪

55
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:34,640
♪ This one-of-a-kind view ♪

56
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:38,380
♪ This feeling of breaking free ♪

57
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:42,110
♪ Nothing can stand in our way ♪

58
00:03:42,130 --> 00:03:43,790
♪ Summer vibe ♪

59
00:03:43,810 --> 00:03:45,400
♪ Summer vibe ♪

60
00:03:45,430 --> 00:03:48,360
♪ In the clear summer sky ♪

61
00:03:48,170 --> 00:03:50,950
[It's Just Business: Episode 4]

62
00:03:48,390 --> 00:03:51,140
♪ Drifting all around, summer vibe ♪

63
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:56,670
Seriously, if you're going to stay out
all night, you should at least text me.

64
00:03:56,670 --> 00:03:59,130
I've been worried sick about you.

65
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:00,870
I'm sorry.

66
00:04:02,690 --> 00:04:05,510
So, how did it go? Was everything okay?

67
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:07,220
Huh?

68
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,950
Well, you know.

69
00:04:08,970 --> 00:04:12,770
When you spend the night together,
isn't that what usually happens?

70
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:17,610
Hey, what's going on?
Are you with your girlfriend right now?

71
00:04:17,610 --> 00:04:21,410
Wow, don't tell me you two
even had morning coffee together.

72
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:24,030
Hey, I told you it's not what you think!

73
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:26,920
I just ended up crashing
at a friend's place.

74
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:28,730
Not this again.

75
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,530
Hey, I'm serious.

76
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:32,070
Ugh, I'm hanging up!

77
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:34,960
Anyway, I'm sorry I didn't text you
last night. Bye.

78
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:36,530
Hey, wait.

79
00:04:54,390 --> 00:04:56,610
He didn't sleep last night?

80
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,330
That means...

81
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:03,670
Oh, you took the bed.

82
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:07,060
So I had to sleep on the sofa
and I barely got any rest.

83
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:10,660
Oh, I'm sorry.

84
00:05:11,410 --> 00:05:14,080
How long have I been asleep?

85
00:05:15,670 --> 00:05:16,910
Well,

86
00:05:18,110 --> 00:05:20,650
about 15 hours.

87
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:24,420
Huh?

88
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:27,330
I was starting to wonder
if you were pregnant.

89
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,080
This is so embarrassing!

90
00:05:31,730 --> 00:05:33,620
I passed out at the arcade, right?

91
00:05:34,470 --> 00:05:35,530
You remember that?

92
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:38,290
Yeah, I have a faint memory of that.

93
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:42,290
-I felt a bit lightheaded at the arcade.
-Are you okay, Ren?

94
00:05:42,290 --> 00:05:44,460
-We need to get you to the hospital!
-No need.

95
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:45,900
Issei.

96
00:05:50,659 --> 00:05:53,020
It's probably just anemia.

97
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,080
I haven't slept much lately.

98
00:05:55,110 --> 00:05:56,180
Ren.

99
00:05:57,470 --> 00:05:59,170
Let him get some rest at my place.

100
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:00,650
I live nearby.

101
00:06:00,670 --> 00:06:01,220
But...

102
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,120
It's fine.

103
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:04,350
If anything happens,
I'll take him straight to the hospital.

104
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:05,680
We'll come with you too.

105
00:06:05,690 --> 00:06:07,140
No need. Sorry.

106
00:06:07,590 --> 00:06:10,770
We were having such a good time. I didn't
expect things to turn out this way.

107
00:06:10,770 --> 00:06:13,340
Ren's health comes first.

108
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:17,210
Come on, let's go.

109
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,420
Is he going to be okay?

110
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:27,090
Wow.

111
00:06:27,110 --> 00:06:30,110
I feel bad for those girls, too.

112
00:06:31,690 --> 00:06:32,950
I bet.

113
00:06:32,970 --> 00:06:33,590
Eh?

114
00:06:34,050 --> 00:06:36,610
Then I took a taxi and brought you here.

115
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:37,630
Oh.

116
00:06:37,650 --> 00:06:40,400
You started dozing off in the taxi,

117
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,920
nd the moment we got here,

118
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,780
you just collapsed onto the bed.

119
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:47,400
I'm really sorry!

120
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,710
What did I do while I was here?

121
00:06:54,290 --> 00:06:55,350
Hey, wait a minute.

122
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:57,659
These aren't my pajamas.

123
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,380
Of course not.

124
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:00,960
Because you're at my place.

125
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,740
So these are...

126
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:10,130
That's right.

127
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:15,900
They're mine.

128
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:20,890
Wh-What?

129
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:25,460
It's like a scene where a girl borrows
her boyfriend's clothes at his place.

130
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:27,270
B-But I...

131
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,230
didn't shower before I fell asleep,

132
00:07:29,230 --> 00:07:31,510
and I don't remember
changing into pajamas.

133
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:32,770
I changed them for you.

134
00:07:34,409 --> 00:07:36,820
Huh? You did?

135
00:07:38,820 --> 00:07:40,350
Who else would it have been?

136
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:43,940
Ah.

137
00:07:46,830 --> 00:07:48,159
Thank goodness.

138
00:07:48,650 --> 00:07:50,960
My chastity is safe...

139
00:07:58,840 --> 00:07:59,690
or is it?

140
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:06,580
Could it be...

141
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,670
Could it be...

142
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:44,039
No, no, no, no!

143
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:46,460
Oh, where's your family?

144
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:47,800
Huh?

145
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:51,180
If he lived with his family, he probably

146
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,060
wouldn't do something like that.

147
00:08:53,090 --> 00:08:56,550
I mean, I just showed up out of nowhere
and ended up staying the night.

148
00:08:56,550 --> 00:08:58,680
I feel bad for putting your family out.

149
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,010
Did they leave for work?

150
00:09:02,590 --> 00:09:03,990
I live alone.

151
00:09:04,490 --> 00:09:05,010
Eh?

152
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:10,310
Here?

153
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:13,500
But Issei, your home is in Tokyo, right?

154
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:14,700
Yes.

155
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:18,360
But this place is closer to school.

156
00:09:19,190 --> 00:09:21,450
Given the location and all this space...

157
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:24,190
the rent can't be cheap.

158
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:27,770
Ah, is your family

159
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:29,210
super rich?

160
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:33,230
It's just a normal family. Why do you ask?

161
00:09:33,350 --> 00:09:35,600
Look,

162
00:09:37,130 --> 00:09:41,190
your family lives in Tokyo, and they pay
for a nice place like this for you.

163
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,800
My family doesn't pay my rent.

164
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,020
What do you mean?

165
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,220
I mean literally what I said.

166
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:50,250
I take care of myself.

167
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:53,600
Really?

168
00:09:56,070 --> 00:09:58,700
But the rent here is expensive, isn't it?

169
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:03,860
What kind of part-time jobs do you have?

170
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,480
Well, quite a few.

171
00:10:10,770 --> 00:10:11,630
Quite a few?

172
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:15,800
But...

173
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:20,140
He says he lives alone, which means...

174
00:11:02,970 --> 00:11:03,820
Ugh!

175
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:04,910
Are you okay?

176
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:05,930
Ah, sorry.

177
00:11:05,950 --> 00:11:08,720
No, no, no, no.

178
00:11:14,130 --> 00:11:15,610
Wait, hold on.

179
00:11:15,710 --> 00:11:18,630
If this guy lives alone
in a place like this,

180
00:11:22,530 --> 00:11:25,130
he could bring anyone home
whenever he wanted.

181
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,930
But does he bring a woman home

182
00:11:31,950 --> 00:11:33,400
or a man?

183
00:11:35,450 --> 00:11:37,050
What's Issei's type anyway?

184
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:43,610
You like me, right?

185
00:11:48,410 --> 00:11:49,590
Let me guess.

186
00:11:51,510 --> 00:11:53,040
You like me, don't you?

187
00:11:57,850 --> 00:11:58,890
Probably.

188
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:02,480
So that means you do like me, right?

189
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,410
If you don't,

190
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,690
just tell me clearly.

191
00:12:27,150 --> 00:12:27,750
I'm sorry.

192
00:12:50,070 --> 00:12:50,850
I...

193
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:54,640
felt like you favored me,

194
00:12:54,660 --> 00:12:56,560
and it gave me this
strange sense of superiority,

195
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:57,480
so...

196
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:00,160
I started reading too much into things.

197
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:15,180
What nonsense am I talking about?

198
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:21,010
Maybe I hit my head when I passed out.
I must've damaged my brain.

199
00:13:24,810 --> 00:13:26,150
I'm such an idiot.

200
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:32,510
Please tell me clearly
that I'm not an idiot,

201
00:13:33,260 --> 00:13:34,690
that I'm not reading too much into things.

202
00:13:34,690 --> 00:13:36,350
Please, just set me straight!

203
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:53,050
Didn't you say it would only happen once?

204
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:08,060
Ren, are you okay?

205
00:14:59,970 --> 00:15:01,570
That's what you said, right?

206
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,450
Just once,

207
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:06,450
and then we should forget about it.

208
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:11,850
I get it.

209
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:15,680
Then let's do it just once.
I'll make you feel good.

210
00:15:16,070 --> 00:15:18,800
Once you're satisfied,
just forget all about it.

211
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,890
-I didn't...
-Didn't you?

212
00:15:34,610 --> 00:15:35,560
Hey.

213
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:38,390
Can I be honest with you?

214
00:15:41,310 --> 00:15:42,910
Wouldn't it bother you

215
00:15:44,850 --> 00:15:46,810
if I said I like you?

216
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:07,370
I don't want to change you,

217
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:10,630
and I don't want to tie you down.

218
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:16,220
I'll never stop you
from going wherever you want.

219
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:18,150
If you want me to follow you, I will.

220
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:24,410
If you want this to be a one-time thing,
I'll accept that too.

221
00:16:27,970 --> 00:16:30,770
I won't do anything
that makes you uncomfortable.

222
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:34,460
You can ask me to do anything.

223
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:39,800
Wouldn't that make you like a puppet?

224
00:16:41,570 --> 00:16:42,490
Exactly.

225
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:49,240
What you felt wasn't
some harmless sense of superiority.

226
00:16:50,580 --> 00:16:52,240
It was a sense of power over me.

227
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:04,560
Only you can control me as you please.

228
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:06,790
Ren.

229
00:17:12,069 --> 00:17:13,270
What do you want to do?

230
00:17:15,940 --> 00:17:17,670
What do you want me to do for you?

231
00:17:20,859 --> 00:17:21,940
I see.

232
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,430
So that's what it is.

233
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:28,640
Lately,

234
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:31,830
I haven't been able to sleep at all.

235
00:17:35,270 --> 00:17:36,130
But...

236
00:17:37,350 --> 00:17:40,020
in this room, I fell asleep so easily.

237
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:44,490
Why is that?

238
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:47,960
Now I finally understand.

239
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:51,090
This warmth,

240
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:52,980
this scent...

241
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:55,620
Just because he's here next to me,

242
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:57,480
and I feel so...

243
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:17,450
Come on.

244
00:19:45,410 --> 00:19:46,710
Ren.

245
00:19:47,750 --> 00:19:48,720
Yeah, okay.

246
00:20:28,190 --> 00:20:29,430
Wait,

247
00:20:29,970 --> 00:20:31,900
I might die from the pain.

248
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:38,050
Then, before you die, I want to tell you:

249
00:20:39,360 --> 00:20:40,500
I like you.

250
00:21:33,870 --> 00:21:35,200
Ah, Issei.

251
00:21:36,130 --> 00:21:37,200
Issei.

252
00:21:53,300 --> 00:21:55,050
I want more.

253
00:21:56,520 --> 00:22:02,140
♪ Countless moments,
added up again and again ♪

254
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:08,190
♪ To create this ordinary miracle
we hold dear ♪

255
00:22:08,250 --> 00:22:14,230
♪ Along the winding paths to freedom ♪

256
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:18,990
♪ Each of us has been given ♪

257
00:22:19,010 --> 00:22:21,990
♪ Right here, right now,
so real and true ♪

258
00:22:22,010 --> 00:22:26,340
♪ The pieces in our hands ♪

259
00:22:26,390 --> 00:22:31,930
♪ Fitting them together, piece by piece ♪

260
00:22:32,060 --> 00:22:38,000
♪ At last, they form a perfect whole ♪

261
00:22:38,030 --> 00:22:41,080
♪ All the pain ♪

262
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:43,890
♪ All the worries ♪

263
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:50,160
♪ Are waiting for the day
we walk hand in hand ♪

264
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:55,370
♪ Waiting for that day ♪

265
00:22:55,940 --> 00:22:58,970
♪ Bit by bit ♪

266
00:22:58,990 --> 00:23:01,890
♪ We put them together ♪

267
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:05,100
♪ Until at last ♪

268
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:08,090
♪ They form a perfect whole ♪

269
00:23:08,110 --> 00:23:11,020
♪ All the pain ♪

270
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:13,810
♪ All the worries ♪

271
00:23:13,830 --> 00:23:20,210
♪ Are waiting for the day
we walk hand in hand ♪

272
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:23,550
♪ Quietly waiting ♪

273
00:23:23,570 --> 00:23:26,240
♪ For the day we walk hand in hand ♪

274
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:29,660
♪ Thoughts fill the page,
along with all that nonsense ♪

275
00:23:26,370 --> 00:23:29,390
[Coming Up Next]

276
00:23:26,870 --> 00:23:29,830
The beach sounds like a nice place to go.

277
00:23:29,690 --> 00:23:33,450
♪ Just one step away from you ♪

278
00:23:29,890 --> 00:23:31,640
Let's go hit on someone!

279
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:34,130
The five of us came here to have fun.

280
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:35,370
♪ Just a gentle leap ♪

281
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,890
If I lose my composure here,

282
00:23:35,390 --> 00:23:37,450
♪ Before summer ends ♪

283
00:23:35,910 --> 00:23:37,200
Issei will pin me down.

284
00:23:37,510 --> 00:23:40,580
♪ I want to leave a mark in your heart ♪

285
00:23:38,070 --> 00:23:39,270
Don't be too upset.

286
00:23:39,290 --> 00:23:41,340
I'm going to fight back at the bar!

287
00:23:40,690 --> 00:23:45,930
♪ A gentle breeze blows,
and in this moment, I pray to the gods ♪

288
00:23:41,370 --> 00:23:43,140
Are you jealous?

289
00:23:42,180 --> 00:23:45,980
[This drama is entirely fictional]

290
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:45,820
This time, it's my turn to dote on him.
